From 952bd37e4bbceda794f3cc823e18f1c0948beeeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:43:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aegisos: mark credential_capture flag READ_ONLY for cp2a
 release config

The cp2a release config (which sdk_phone64_x86_64-cp2a-userdebug and
lynx-cur-userdebug both build against) sets
RELEASE_ACONFIG_REQUIRE_ALL_READ_ONLY=true (inherited from bp1a's own
flag_values/bp1a/RELEASE_ACONFIG_REQUIRE_ALL_READ_ONLY.textproto),
which Soong turns into --allow-read-write false on every
'aconfig create-cache' invocation for this release config
(build/soong/aconfig/aconfig_declarations.go). A flag_value with
permission: READ_WRITE is rejected outright by the aconfig tool under
that flag, confirmed by a real build failure:

  Error: failed to create cache
  Caused by:
      flag credential_capture has permission READ_WRITE, but
      allow_read_write is false

Every other *_flag_values.textproto already checked into
aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/ uses permission: READ_ONLY - this file
was the only outlier, carried over unchanged from the original
trunk_staging placement without re-checking whether READ_WRITE was
still valid once the value actually reached a release config that
enforces this policy. READ_ONLY is also the correct choice on the
merits here: this flag only needs to be permanently baked in as
enabled at build time, not toggleable post-build via aflags/
device_config - and READ_ONLY is arguably the safer choice for a
security-relevant behavior change, since it cannot be flipped off at
runtime by anyone with device_config write access.
---
 .../android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto  | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto b/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
index 28a0d4cc5..f18ae512b 100644
--- a/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
+++ b/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
@@ -2,5 +2,5 @@ flag_value {
   package: "android.multiuser"
   name: "credential_capture"
   state: ENABLED
-  permission: READ_WRITE
+  permission: READ_ONLY
 }
-- 
2.39.5

